[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118733082,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118779566,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.11878491,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118789286,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118793131,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118797016,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118800798,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118804543,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118807936,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118811456,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118815031,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118819034,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below 12 qubits (8 with mid-circuit measurement), and the CI gate shards (`kaggle_run.py shards`) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118824986,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches 12 qubits, or 8 with mid-circuit measurement (docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md, \"CPU against T4\") | IBM jobs; narrow replays, which the T4 speeds up by at most 3 times |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.11882972,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118833825,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. An account without Persona identity verification gets a 4-core CPU machine for every TPU request; a verified account's request queues for a TPU, one batch session at a time (docs/notes/kaggle/tpu-research.md) | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118838617,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118842966,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118847464,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118851642,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118856114,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118859834,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118863634,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118869002,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118883659,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118907615,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118914267,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118917911,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118927858,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118931794,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack, built and proved by\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118935415,"data":"   `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`. `--fetch` downloads the seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118938988,"data":"   archives `RELEASES` pins and keeps each only if its sha256 matches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118942677,"data":"   `--install` installs sixteen of them with `pip install --no-deps`,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118946388,"data":"   applying `BUILD_RECIPES` (the cayley-dickson, SplitOct and pyquaternion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118950037,"data":"   PKGBUILD `prepare()` steps) and taking the Octonion-Sedenion wheel as\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118953978,"data":"   published, then installs `RUNTIME_PINS`: numpy-quaternion, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118957714,"data":"   seventeenth, as its pinned compiled wheel, and numba, sparse and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118961182,"data":"   anywidget. `--extract` binds all seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118964693,"data":"   installed distributions to their archives and regenerates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118968511,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json`; the kernel stops with exit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118971954,"data":"   code 3 unless those bytes equal the retained ones. The build host passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118975819,"data":"   the same test against its Arch packages, so a run that reaches its entry\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118979553,"data":"   used the same algebra code as the host. The file's `packages` field\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118983248,"data":"   records the versions `kernel_main.REPORTED_PACKAGES` names, nine of the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118986694,"data":"   seventeen algebra distributions; the byte comparison binds the rest.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118990344,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118994019,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.118997543,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119001466,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119004764,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119008114,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119011423,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119014918,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119018183,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.11902168,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119025322,"data":"| cuquantum-cu11 | 24.8.0 (brings custatevec-cu11 1.6.0.post1 and cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0; the libraries the cu11 Aer wheel links) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119029161,"data":"| cutensor-cu11 | 2.2.0 (the newest release inside cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0's `\u003e=2.0.1,\u003c3`) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119034199,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119037778,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119044671,"data":"| quaternionic, clifford, kingdon, galgebra, pyoctonion | 1.0.18, 1.5.1, 3.0.0, 0.6.0, 3.12 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119048514,"data":"| pyquaternion | 0.9.9 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe (writes the VERSION.txt the sdist omits) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119052058,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119055447,"data":"| hyprat | 0.2.0 | GitHub tag archive, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119058903,"data":"| Octonion-Sedenion | 1.0.0 | PyPI wheel (its only release form), sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119062445,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI compiled wheel at the pin; `--extract` binds its Python files to the sha256-pinned sdist (Octonion-Sedenion builds on it) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119066635,"data":"| numba, sparse, anywidget | 0.68.0, 0.17.0, 0.11.0 | PyPI (`RUNTIME_PINS`; runtime dependencies of quaternionic, clifford and kingdon) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119069934,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119073204,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119076441,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119079509,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119082731,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119085969,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119089451,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119092783,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119096191,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119099479,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119102444,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119105614,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119109346,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119112474,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119116003,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119119086,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119122565,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119125595,"data":"- An entry whose output a CI gate recompiles runs with `push --ci-env` on a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119128804,"data":"  CPU or GPU machine, using CPU Aer either way. The kernel then builds CI's Python 3.14.7 with CI's pins\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119133534,"data":"  through `ci/install_pins.sh` and runs the entry under it, because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119137258,"data":"  image's Python 3.13 and numpy 2.1.3 change compiled depths and durations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119143677,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119146718,"data":"## Aer on the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119149956,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119153036,"data":"- **Requesting a GPU.** Push with `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4` and a `--timeout`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119156445,"data":"  sized to the work; kaggle_run.py refuses an accelerator push without one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119159736,"data":"  The kernel installs qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 0.17.2, cuquantum-cu11 24.8.0 and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119162891,"data":"  cutensor-cu11 2.2.0 and sets `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE=GPU`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119166203,"data":"- **cuStateVec.** `noise_simulator(..., custatevec=True)` sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119169496,"data":"  `cuStateVec_enable` on a GPU statevector run; `scripts/aer_gpu_probe.py\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119172731,"data":"  --workloads n21 --configurations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119192992,"data":"  cpu_statevector,gpu_statevector_unbatched,gpu_statevector_custatevec` records\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119196681,"data":"  the three paths with Aer's reported `cuStateVec_enable`. The option excludes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119200162,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`. `docs/notes/kaggle/custatevec.md` holds the library\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119203692,"data":"  chain, the T4 push command and how to read its result.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119207326,"data":"- **Using it in an entry.** The entry passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119210756,"data":"  `calibration_snapshot.aer_device()` to `noise_simulator(snapshot, device,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119214434,"data":"  method=...)`. On a GPU the simulator batches shots of circuits of at most\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119217757,"data":"  10 active qubits without control flow and runs feed-forward circuits shot\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119221432,"data":"  by shot (`calibration_snapshot.SnapshotSimulator`).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119225002,"data":"- **Noise model width.** Restricting the snapshot and the circuit to the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119228513,"data":"  active qubits (`snapshot_laws.restrict` and `restrict_circuit`) keeps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119231968,"data":"  Aer's noise model at the circuit's width on either device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119235327,"data":"- **What the GPU is for.** It pays for density matrices at\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119238642,"data":"  `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` (11) qubits or more and for wide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119242338,"data":"  statevectors. Small dynamic circuits sample faster on the host CPUs. On\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119245766,"data":"  the 7-qubit N=21 order-finding circuits, statevector trajectories took 2.8\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119249176,"data":"  and 36 ms per shot on the CPU, against 21.7 and 54.6 ms on one T4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119252668,"data":"- **Batched shots.** `noise_simulator(..., batched_shots=True)` enables Aer's\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119255985,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`, which aborts on any circuit with control flow\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119259469,"data":"  (`if_else` lowers to `jump`), so only static circuits may batch. Batched\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119263074,"data":"  static runs are unmeasured here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119267405,"data":"- **Replay.** A GPU's seeded counts differ from the CPU's. Its records are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119274998,"data":"  replayed from their retained counts, never by resampling on CI.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119278396,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119281429,"data":"The measurements are in `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`, from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.119285103,"data":"`results/kaggle/2026-10-16T204620Z-gororoba-aer-gpu-probe`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":50.11928841,"data":"\n"}
